    "solution": "Begin at full tide and cross the submerged thorn reef. In the narrow sluice well, swim beneath the broad stone and dash upward into it. It parks against the visible overhead stop, opening the side passage into the basin. Approach the float from its side, climb onto it and jump to the gallery above normal swimming height. Strike the hinged partition at its hub; the former wall becomes a horizontal walk into the eastern yard. Hop and cut down onto the broad anvil to reach the tally balcony. Return across the turned arm. The sea has now exposed the lower reef, so drop onto the same stone that you raised out of the well, pause there and jump into the upper western gallery. The final walk is sheltered and level.",
    "nearestExisting": "B13 manufactures a stopper for a horizontal block; B12 trades a beam shield for a bridge; the original Landing Shores rooms use tidal floats for launch timing. This room uses submerged thorns to permit access below a full-width sluice stone. Its upward displacement simultaneously opens the wet outward route and leaves a permanent dry stair for a return directly above that route. No lantern transport or optical circuit is involved.",
    "novelty": "The water changes which face of the heavy object is reachable. The stone stays where the knight sent it after the enabling water has gone, so its second job survives the tide. The tall hinged partition becomes a reusable crossing, and the float can be left behind once it has delivered the knight above swimming height.",
