    "interconnection": "Two western passages are vertically stacked around one well: a flooded thorn tunnel outward and a dry upper exit home. Moving the same visible stone connects these paths. The tide and float govern access to a persistent hinged opening, which the knight traverses in both directions.",
    "superroom": {
      "screenAreas": 3.8260869565217392,
      "stages": [
        "Flooded reef and underside of the sluice",
        "Float, hinged gallery and anvil balcony",
        "Return on the same raised stone above the dry reef"
      ]
    },
    "entrance": "West low chamber; the first full tide already covers the thorn reef.",
    "exit": "West upper gallery, directly over the outbound tunnel.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The return stone offers a stable rest before a 16-pixel rise into a 32-tile sheltered gallery. A three-second rest on the stone and a two-frame earlier sideways input both finish without deaths. The far tally balcony is eight tiles wide; missing its anvil transfer drops to a broad safe yard. No final swing, moving catch or momentum chain is required.",
    "designNotes": "The tide intentionally uses reversed endpoints: low=20 is the initial full-water hold, high=38 is the ebb hold. Existing periodic interpolation supports this without runtime changes. It removes an otherwise empty opening wait while preserving a full-water outward route and dry return. A missed float cycle can be waited out safely in the sluice basin. The canonical route uses ordinary Base dash, swimming, climbing, jumping and anvil pogo.",
